    description: "Found by the 2026-10-05 docstring staleness audit (reviewer reproduced): fmt.println(...) yields two unresolved edges, one to fmt.println and one to println. Fix: skip a call_expression whose parent member_expression the member handler consumes; fixture asserting one edge per member call."  # dbd5
    fields:  # dbd5
      statement: "One call site produces one call edge."  # dbd5
      root_cause: "In tree-sitter-odin, obj.method(args) is a member_expression wrapping a call_expression (odin.py ~L320-330), so the plain call handler (~L287-318) also fires on the inner call and emits an edge to the bare method name."  # dbd5
